            <ArticleTitle>Hepatocellular carcinoma in two captive golden-headed lion tamarins (Leontopithecus chrysomelas).</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jmp.12324</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) in 2 female captive golden-headed lion tamarins (Leontopithecus chrysomelas) are described. HCC was diagnosed in both, with pulmonary metastasis in one of them. Neoplastic cells were positive for hepatocyte-specific antigen (HSA) by immunohistochemistry, confirming the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
